## Autonomy

- Complete the requested work through implementation, verification, fixes, and a local commit. Continue through routine steps and plan phases without confirmation.
- Routine project edits, dependency changes, tests, builds, network access, development services, and disposable cleanup are authorized. Route eligible permission requests through automatic review when the harness supports it.
- Pause before destructive or irreversible actions, including database deletion, infrastructure teardown, loss of user work, and irreversible changes to shared systems. Name the action, target, and effect before asking.
- Ask when a decision cannot be resolved from project evidence. Diagnose recoverable failures and continue independent authorized work while a decision is pending. A timeout is not approval.
- A permission denial or a secret exposure stops the blocked action. Report it and continue only independent authorized work. Never retry the denied outcome through another route.
- Never read credentials, bypass a deny, or change live agent permissions to unblock yourself. A command no deny rule matches is not thereby allowed.
- Inspect cleanup targets. Preserve unknown files and persistent storage.
